            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0006",
              "severity": "low",
              "cvss": 3.7,
              "timestamp": "2026-10-25 15:43:46 UTC",
              "target": "cra-scan (src/matcher.py)",
              "endpoint": "src/matcher.py::evaluate",
              "method": "N/A",
              "cwe": "CWE-754",
              "impact": "An affected component with an unanswered OSV query and a KEV-listed CVE is shown with exploited False and exploited_known True, and its action is HUMAN_REVIEW instead of URGENT_HUMAN_REVIEW. The output asserts a check that did not happen. The run is still marked RESULT INCOMPLETE, so the operator is warned, but the per-finding urgency and the stored finding record are wrong.",
              "technical_analysis": "evaluate hands every finding an exploited_known flag. For findings with a usable CVE list, the flag is computed from the KEV freshness and from invalid evidence files. For three paths the code passes the KEV freshness itself, although no CVE of the component was looked up:\n\n```python title=src/matcher.py startLineNumber=396 endLineNumber=396\n            findings.append(_finding(component, None, UNKNOWN, \"osv_gave_no_answer\", exploited_known=kev_ok))\n```\n\nThe same pattern appears at line 401 (osv_details_missing) and line 413 (record_malformed). With a fresh KEV list, `exploited_known` becomes True, and `action_for` then returns HUMAN_REVIEW for an UNKNOWN finding. The code's own rule for the KEV-failed case is that an unchecked exploitation status must be urgent (test_failed_kev_download_never_turns_into_not_exploited expects URGENT_HUMAN_REVIEW), so the same state is handled inconsistently depending on whether the KEV feed failed or OSV failed. The paths on the same lines are reached when the purl has no OSV answer, when a listed advisory cannot be downloaded or validated, or when the advisory cannot be evaluated.",
              "remediation_steps": "On the three paths where no CVE list was obtained (no OSV answer, advisory details missing, and an advisory that cannot be evaluated), record exploited_known as False, so the finding follows the same urgent-review rule that already applies to a failed KEV download. Apply the same invariant to components without a purl, which currently pass the KEV freshness as well; that change alters the urgency of every component without a purl, so the maintainers should confirm it as product policy before it is made.",
              "counterevidence": "The CLI prints RESULT INCOMPLETE for any run with an OSV failure and warns about data gaps, and the exit code is non-zero, so the operator is warned that the run is not trustworthy. The change only affects the urgency label and the stored exploited_known value, not the exploited flag or the affected status. A KEV-listed CVE for a component whose OSV answer is missing would still not be found, which is an OSV data gap rather than a matcher decision. Components without a purl are the same invariant but are left as a policy question.",
              "confidence": "high",
              "severity_change_conditions": "Evidence that the run summary alone is used for triage (so the per-finding action is never read) would not raise the rating, while evidence that a KEV-listed affected component routinely has an OSV no-answer at run time would raise it to medium.",
              "fix_verification": "Gate 1 (applicability): three single-line changes at src/matcher.py:396, 401 and 413; the file compiles (python3 -m py_compile). Gate 2 (security closure): the PoC now prints exploited_known False and URGENT_HUMAN_REVIEW for both the no-answer and details-missing states. Gate 3 (bypass review): the remaining sibling is the component_unknown path (line 391), which still passes the KEV freshness; it is the same invariant but changes the urgency of every component without a purl, so it is deliberately left as a product decision. The normal path at line 416 is unchanged: a checked advisory has a real KEV result, so its flag remains valid. Gate 4 (preserved behavior): the exploited flag, status, rule and the failed-KEV behaviour are unchanged; the existing KEV-failed test still passes. Gate 5 (repository checks): python3 -m pytest -q tests gives 408 passed, 2 skipped. Not run: an end-to-end CLI run with a real OSV failure, and bandit.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Run from the repository root with the project's Python environment.\n2. Build a component for pkg:maven/org.apache.logging.log4j/log4j-core@2.14.1 and a feed set where OSV gave no answer for that purl (purl_vulns value None), with a fresh KEV list that contains CVE-2021-44228.\n3. Run the CRA evaluation step and read the single finding.\n4. The correct record marks exploited_known as False and the action as URGENT_HUMAN_REVIEW, because the component's CVEs were never checked against KEV.\n5. Repeat with the advisory listed but its details missing (vulns value None) to see the same result.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
