          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Terminal escape / control-character and bidi injection from SBOM strings — Ruled out: run/check-sbom output: SBOM-derived name, version, purl, group (src/sbom_reader.py _clean/_read_component; cli.py _describe, _check_sbom)\n\nThe control is the strict ASCII allow-list in sbom_reader.py (NAME_PATTERN, VERSION_PATTERN, PURL_PATTERN, GROUP via _clean, fullmatch after strip(\" \") only). A component with ESC/CR/bidi in name, version, purl or group becomes UNKNOWN with name/version/purl dropped to None ('(unnamed)', '?'), and check-sbom/run output contains no control bytes (work/exp1.out). _describe and _check_sbom print these fields without printable(), so this pattern check is the only control on that path; it is currently sufficient (gap noted: defense-in-depth only, not exploitable today)."
