        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/failed-run-record-path-handling-error-text-persistence-file-name-control",
          "ruleIndex": 25,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Failed-run record path handling, error-text persistence, file-name control — No issue identified: _save_failed_run and save_run (cli.py _save_failed_run; news_watcher.py save_run, _write_json_atomic) - path handling and error text\n\nFile name is built only from now() (save_run), never from input, so no traversal. A forced RuntimeError containing a path and a token produced a record with only error='RuntimeError' (work/exp6): no message text persisted or printed. Cache-as-file gives failed record with NotADirectoryError name (exp5a). Unwritable runs path prints 'could NOT be saved' (exp5b). Existing directory at stamp name -> suffix -0002 (exp5c). Temp file via mkstemp in the same folder and os.replace is atomic. Minor, not reported: two runs in the same second can race between path.exists() and os.replace, so one run record can be overwritten (sub-second window, same data)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
