          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Information disclosure (paths, cache layout, identifiers) — No issue identified: Information disclosure in run/status output and run records: absolute folder paths, cache layout, product and SBOM fingerprint (cli._run Folders/Run saved lines; run record 'folders', 'sbom_sha256', 'product')\n\nstatus output contains no paths and no cache layout. run prints cache/runs/evidence paths and 'Run saved:' path, which are the operator's own inputs to their own terminal. Run record stores absolute folder paths (folders.cache/runs/evidence) and the product config with the SBOM sha256. This is local, operator-owned data; it is not sent, and it contains no secret or credential. Low sensitivity: a copy of a run record shared outside the team would reveal the local folder layout and user name in the path. Not reported as a finding."
