          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/unaffected-component-reported-affected-false-positive-and-unknown-answers-turned-into-not-affected",
          "ruleIndex": 29,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "unaffected component reported AFFECTED (false positive) and unknown answers turned into NOT_AFFECTED — No issue identified: matcher._check_entry / _check_entry_maven / _check_entry_pypi (AFFECTED decision, exact version lists, unknown fallbacks)\n\nDifferential fuzz of match_vulnerability over about 113k ECOSYSTEM range/version comparisons (PyPI with packaging, Maven with pre-release limits) against an independent state-machine reference: 0 false positives. Maven exact-list match is raw-string equality (so \"2.0.0\" vs listed \"2.0\" yields UNKNOWN, not NOT_AFFECTED; conservative). Unreadable limits, non-plain Maven versions and unreadable PyPI versions all return UNKNOWN (matcher.py:165-179, 185-187). Under evaluate() the osv_listed guard prevents NOT_AFFECTED output. Existing 100 matcher tests pass, and the patched copy passes the full suite (408 passed, 2 skipped)."
          },
          "locations": [
