        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/range-type-not-evaluated-but-reported-as-not-affected",
          "ruleIndex": 30,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "range type not evaluated but reported as NOT_AFFECTED — Ruled out: matcher._in_intervals / _usable_ranges / _unsupported_range_types (GIT, SEMVER and mixed ranges)\n\nNamed control: match_vulnerability (matcher.py:243-251) checks every matching entry for AFFECTED first, then UNKNOWN, and only then checks _unsupported_range_types. Any GIT or non-ECOSYSTEM range on a matching entry therefore converts a NOT_AFFECTED result to UNKNOWN (git_range_not_supported or range_type_not_supported), and a version-list-only entry is still gated by the same check. Verified with a SEMVER range next to a good range (UNKNOWN) and the GIT+ECOSYSTEM fixture PYSEC-2023-74 (UNKNOWN for 2.31.0, AFFECTED for 2.30.0)."
          },
          "locations": [
