        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/wrong-version-ordering-text-comparison-trailing-zeros-pre-release-oversized-numbers",
          "ruleIndex": 31,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "wrong version ordering (text comparison, trailing zeros, pre-release, oversized numbers) — No issue identified: matcher.maven_version_key / maven_limit_key / _numbers (Maven numeric comparison and pre-release limits)\n\nVersions are never compared as text: PLAIN_VERSION fullmatch (matcher.py:63) then integer tuples. Trailing zeros are stripped (2.0 == 2.0.0, checked). Pre-release limits (2.0-beta9, -rc, -alpha, -m) map to just below the release, and this stays correct for plain components because plain versions never fall between them. Numbers longer than 9 digits and any qualifier outside the pattern return None, which becomes UNKNOWN. Maven differential fuzz with pre-release limits: 0 false positives and 0 false negatives after the same-version ordering fix (about 78k comparisons)."
          },
          "locations": [
