        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/pypi-version-or-name-mismatch-causing-wrong-affected-not-affected-result",
          "ruleIndex": 32,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "PyPI version or name mismatch causing wrong affected/not-affected result — No issue identified: matcher._pypi_version / normalize_pypi_name (PyPI version parsing and PEP 503 names)\n\nVersions use packaging.Version (PEP 440 ordering, pre/dev/post). Names apply PEP 503 (-, _, . collapse, lowercase) to both the SBOM purl and the OSV package name (matcher.py:46-48, 218). Fuzz over PyPI ranges shows 0 false positives. Known deviation, deliberate and tested: a local build (1.0+abc) is read as release 1.0 (matcher.py:86). This is conservative for fixed boundaries but can include a local build of last_affected (1.0+abc counted as affected); no real feed sample exercised it, so it is noted, not reported."
          },
