            "text": "purl namespace or type confusion matching the wrong package or version — Ruled out: matcher._package_identity / _entry_matches (purl type, namespace, qualifiers, name matching)\n\nNamed controls upstream of every CLI path: sbom_reader.py:133-156 rejects purl qualifiers outside its allow-list, rejects a PyPI purl with a namespace, rejects a Maven purl with no namespace, rejects a purl whose namespace/name/version disagree with the SBOM fields, and rebuilds a canonical purl. Only OK components reach the matcher. Inside the matcher, Maven requires group and artifact (exact match on group:artifact), PyPI names are normalized, and ecosystem strings must equal Maven or PyPI exactly. Probed: pkg:maven/log4j-core@2.14.1 is rejected as unsupported; unknown types are UNKNOWN."
