        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/kev-attribution-through-a-related-cve-link-that-is-not-the-same-vulnerability",
          "ruleIndex": 34,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "KEV attribution through a related CVE link that is not the same vulnerability — Requires further review: matcher.exploited_status / cve_ids_of (KEV match through alias and upstream CVE links)\n\ncve_ids_of accepts CVE ids from id, aliases and upstream (matcher.py:260-270), so an advisory whose upstream field names a KEV-listed CVE is marked exploited (matched_on reports \"upstream\"). Not confirmed as wrong: the reading of OSV upstream as the same vulnerability is a data-model judgment, and no saved OSV fixture has a populated upstream field, so the frequency with which upstream names a different CVE could not be tested offline. Matched_on is exposed in the finding so a reviewer can see the link source."
