        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/evidence-file-forces-exploited-true-or-suppresses-it-or-a-missing-or-broken-file-is-treated-as-known-not-exploited",
          "ruleIndex": 35,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "evidence file forces exploited=True or suppresses it, or a missing or broken file is treated as known not-exploited — Ruled out: matcher.exploited_status / read_evidence / invalid_evidence_cves (evidence override direction, missing, stale, future-dated files)\n\nNamed controls: exploited_status checks KEV first and only then evidence, and evidence can only set exploited=True (matcher.py:329-333); there is no path where evidence clears a KEV hit. A missing file returns None (matcher.py:282-283) and leaves exploited False with exploited_known taken from KEV freshness, so a failed KEV download still gives URGENT (test_failed_kev_download_never_turns_into_not_exploited). Broken JSON, non-https link, missing date, future date and non-ISO date return None and are flagged via invalid_evidence_cves (matcher.py:411, 416) which forces exploited_known False. Evidence has no expiry by design (dated, operator-curated); a stale file keeps its exploited flag, which is a policy choice rather than a matcher error."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "matcher.exploited_status / read_evidence / invalid_evidence_cves (evidence override direction, missing, stale, future-dated files)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
