          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "range upper bound silently dropped, widening the affected range to unbounded — Requires further review: matcher._intervals ECOSYSTEM 'limit' events (and unknown event kinds)\n\nObserved: an ECOSYSTEM range [introduced 0, limit 2.0] makes 3.0 AFFECTED because the limit event is silently ignored (not counted as an end, and not treated as unreadable). Not confirmed as a wrong result: whether OSV intends limit as an affected bound or only a search bound for ECOSYSTEM ranges could not be checked offline (no OSV schema copy in the sandbox, web search unavailable), and no saved feed uses limit. If real ECOSYSTEM data can carry it, unknown events should make the range UNKNOWN rather than open-ended."
