            "text": "Host confusion (userinfo, fragment, backslash, subdomain, IP, uppercase, http scheme, non-443 port) — Ruled out: news_watcher.http_fetch host, scheme and port allow-list (ALLOWED_HOSTS check)\n\nNamed control: parsed.scheme != \"https\" / parsed.hostname not in ALLOWED_HOSTS / port not in (None, 443) check runs before any socket is opened (news_watcher.py http_fetch). Tested without network for api.osv.dev@evil, api.osv.dev.evil, evil#@api.osv.dev, http://, [::1], 127.0.0.1, //api.osv.dev, api.osv.dev\\@evil: all refused with 'address is not on the allowed list'. Only the uppercase and :443 variants of the real host passed the check (they reached the public API, which returned 405 to a GET)."
