            "text": "purl/name/version confusion making a component match or miss a vulnerability (non-maven) — Ruled out: sbom_reader._read_component purl/name/version identity checks (version field vs purl version, name vs purl name, PyPI normalization)\n\nControl: _read_component requires parsed.version == version field exactly (sbom_reader.py version mismatch branch) and _same_name for PyPI (PEP 503 normalization) or exact equality for Maven, so name and version fields cannot disagree with the purl identity that the matcher uses. Fuzzed 30000 purl/name/version combinations with 0 exceptions. PyPI spelling variants resolve to the same OSV answer (pkg:pypi/Django, django, django@1.11.0 all returned 49 advisories live), so PyPI case and separator variants cannot hide a component."
