          "message": {
            "text": "Malformed or type-confused KEV feed accepted and used — Ruled out: news_watcher.validate_kev structural checks (types, count, cveID pattern, duplicates, dateAdded, entry shape)\n\nNamed controls in validate_kev: required keys, dateReleased must parse as tz-aware time, vulnerabilities must be a non-empty list of at least MIN_KEV_ENTRIES objects, count must be a non-bool int equal to len, cveID must fullmatch CVE_PATTERN and be unique, dateAdded must be a real date (news_watcher.py validate_kev). Existing tests cover each rejection; a malformed list cannot replace the saved copy because fetch_kev saves only after validate_kev passes. The omission and replay gaps are not in this structural layer and are reported separately (vuln-0007, vuln-0008)."
