        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/symlink-or-path-tricks-reading-or-writing-outside-intended-folders",
          "ruleIndex": 49,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "symlink or path tricks reading or writing outside intended folders — Ruled out: --evidence, --sbom and --config symlink and path handling (safe_join, _read_limited, read_evidence, invalid_evidence_cves)\n\nAttacker-supplied SBOM and feed content never form a path: purl caches use a SHA-256 name, OSV ids go through VULN_ID_PATTERN and safe_join, CVE evidence names pass CVE_PATTERN and safe_join (safe_paths.py resolves the target and rejects a parent that differs from the folder, so an evidence symlink pointing out of the folder is refused). Live test: evidence/CVE-2021-44228.json symlinked to a file outside the folder gives read_evidence None. --sbom and --config are operator-chosen paths; a symlink there is followed, which is the operator's own choice (not attacker reachable). Observation for the operator, not an attacker path: such a refused evidence file is silently ignored rather than reported as unusable, because invalid_evidence_cves swallows the ValueError from safe_join."
          },
          "locations": [
