        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/version-confusion-that-makes-a-component-match-or-miss-a-vulnerability-matcher-logic",
          "ruleIndex": 50,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "version confusion that makes a component match or miss a vulnerability (matcher logic) — Requires further review: SBOM version strings through matcher range checks (PEP 440 local labels, Maven leading zeros, pre-release limits) - handoff to Matcher Logic Agent\n\nHandoff to Matcher Logic Agent. _pypi_version (src/matcher.py) strips the PEP 440 local label, so pkg:pypi/x@2.19.0+anything is evaluated as 2.19.0. Under strict PEP 440 this over-reports (2.19.0+local is greater than 2.19.0 and can be unaffected), so it is not a silent miss in the observed direction; the matcher owner should decide whether it is intended. Maven 2.014.1 normalizes to 2.14.1 numerically; OSV also lists both spellings, so no miss was observed. Not tested end-to-end against every OSV range shape."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
