          "message": {
            "text": "Vulnerability id to file-name traversal or device-name abuse — Ruled out: news_watcher._vuln_cache_path with crafted OSV ids (NUL, unicode lookalikes, absolute, dot segments, Windows device names, percent-encoding)\n\nNamed controls: VULN_ID_PATTERN fullmatch (ASCII class, no '..') and safe_join (src/safe_paths.py: SAFE_NAME fullmatch, no '..', no trailing dot, device-name check, resolved parent must equal the base). Dynamic: 33 crafted ids (../, absolute, NUL, \\n, fullwidth dots U+FF0E, U+2025, backslash, %2e%2e, CON/NUL) were all rejected or confined to the cache folder. Only the trailing-dot case escaped as an uncaught error (filed as vuln-0011); no write occurred outside the cache."
