        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/unbounded-read-of-attacker-supplied-file-toctou",
          "ruleIndex": 53,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "unbounded read of attacker-supplied file, TOCTOU — Ruled out: cli._run SBOM sha256 re-read (Path(args.sbom).read_bytes) after parsing\n\nThe file is the operator-chosen --sbom path, not attacker-chosen content. The parse path already enforces the 10 MB cap through _read_limited before the re-read. Only a file that grows or is swapped between the two reads would differ, which needs local write access to the operator's own file, so no attacker-reachable unbounded read was found."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
