              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/cache-poisoning-a-crafted-purl-overwrites-or-is-read-as-another-component-s-answer",
          "ruleIndex": 55,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Cache poisoning: a crafted purl overwrites or is read as another component's answer — Ruled out: news_watcher._purl_cache_path and fetch_osv purl answer cache (cross-entry poisoning via crafted purl)\n\nNamed controls: cache file name is sha256(purl), so distinct purls map to distinct files; a saved answer is used only when its stored 'purl' equals the requested purl and every id passes VULN_ID_PATTERN (news_watcher.py fetch_osv). SBOM purls are ASCII-only (sbom_reader PURL_PATTERN), so no crafted non-ASCII key reaches the hash. Remote feed input cannot write a cache entry under another purl's name. Precision: a local file copied under another name is rejected by the purl field check unless the operator-local file is also edited to match, which needs write access to the cache folder (operator-controlled per the threat model). Feed-side answer shifting is in the separate needs_follow_up entry."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "news_watcher._purl_cache_path and fetch_osv purl answer cache (cross-entry poisoning via crafted purl)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Cache poisoning: a crafted purl overwrites or is read as another component's answer",
              "surface": "news_watcher._purl_cache_path and fetch_osv purl answer cache (cross-entry poisoning via crafted purl)",
              "recorded_by": "Feed Fetch and Cache Agent",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/feed-returns-a-record-for-one-vulnerability-id-but-content-for-another-or-poisons-a-cache-entry-under-a-different-id",
          "ruleIndex": 56,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Feed returns a record for one vulnerability id but content for another, or poisons a cache entry under a different id — Ruled out: news_watcher.fetch_osv vulnerability record cache and detail download (record id vs requested id)\n\nNamed control: _validate_vuln_record requires record['id'] == requested id before a record is cached or used (news_watcher.py _validate_vuln_record, called for fresh and saved records). Dynamic: a detail response for CVE-2024-0999 served under CVE-2024-0100 was rejected and nothing was written to the cache folder; the vulnerability became 'could not load details' (status failed). Existing test test_osv_record_with_the_wrong_id_is_rejected covers the same path."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
