              "surface": "news_watcher.fetch_osv vulnerability record cache and detail download (record id vs requested id)",
              "recorded_by": "Feed Fetch and Cache Agent",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/answers-for-one-component-attributed-to-another-if-the-feed-reorders-results",
          "ruleIndex": 57,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Answers for one component attributed to another if the feed reorders results — Requires further review: news_watcher.fetch_osv positional mapping of batch answers to purls (_query_purls zip(order, parsed))\n\nBatch results are zipped to the request order by position and only the result count is checked (news_watcher.py _query_purls). No independent control binds a result to its query. Exploiting it needs the same on-path feed position as vuln-0007, so it was not reported separately. Not tested end to end; I did not confirm an attributable impact beyond the feed-trust precondition. Open for the parent to decide whether to test or accept as a feed-trust residual."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "news_watcher.fetch_osv positional mapping of batch answers to purls (_query_purls zip(order, parsed))"
