              "risk_area": "Answers for one component attributed to another if the feed reorders results",
              "surface": "news_watcher.fetch_osv positional mapping of batch answers to purls (_query_purls zip(order, parsed))",
              "recorded_by": "Feed Fetch and Cache Agent",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/unbounded-paging-or-request-volume-from-a-hostile-osv-feed",
          "ruleIndex": 58,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unbounded paging or request volume from a hostile OSV feed — No issue identified: news_watcher._query_purls paging, chunking and detail request caps\n\nCode review: MAX_PAGE_ROUNDS=20 per batch, BATCH_SIZE=500 purls per request, MAX_IDS_PER_PURL=500, MAX_DETAIL_REQUESTS=3000 and per-response size caps bound the request count and memory. A hostile page loop ends with no answer for that chunk (existing test test_osv_page_loop_that_never_ends_gives_no_answer). Time per request is the separate deadline finding (vuln-0009)."
          },
          "locations": [
