        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/type-confusion-or-crash-from-malformed-osv-batch-and-record-fields",
          "ruleIndex": 59,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Type confusion or crash from malformed OSV batch and record fields — Ruled out: news_watcher._parse_batch_result and slim_osv_record (feed-supplied ids, modified, aliases, affected lists)\n\nNamed controls: _parse_batch_result type-checks result, vulns, items, ids and tokens and raises FetchError (caught by _query_purls); slim_osv_record copies only length-capped strings and filtered alias ids, dropping summary, details and references. Dynamic: a trailing-dot id is the only id class that escaped (vuln-0011). Non-string modified and oversized lists were handled by the existing tests and the type checks."
          },
          "locations": [
