        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/partial-or-torn-cache-reads-temp-file-leftovers-races-between-reader-and-writer",
          "ruleIndex": 60,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Partial or torn cache reads; temp file leftovers; races between reader and writer — Ruled out: news_watcher._write_json_atomic and _read_json (temp file handling, concurrent readers during replace)\n\nNamed controls: temp file is created with mkstemp in the target folder and moved with os.replace, which is atomic on the same filesystem; the temp is removed on any exception (news_watcher.py _write_json_atomic). Dynamic: 3 reader threads against 4 writer threads over 240 writes read 267 times with zero reads that saw no valid JSON; no temp files were left in the folder; a failing serialization left no temp file. Killed-process leftovers (.tmp names) are not read by any loader, since loaders match only *.json."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "news_watcher._write_json_atomic and _read_json (temp file handling, concurrent readers during replace)"
                }
