        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/tls-verification-disabled-or-downgraded-allowing-an-unverified-on-path-response",
          "ruleIndex": 63,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "TLS verification disabled or downgraded, allowing an unverified on-path response — No issue identified: news_watcher.http_fetch TLS certificate and hostname verification\n\nCode review: no ssl module use, no custom SSLContext, no CERT_NONE or check_hostname override anywhere under src/, so urllib's default context (certificate and hostname verification on) is used. Dynamic: every test relied on the local server's certificate being trusted through SSL_CERT_FILE, which shows the default trust store is consulted. The on-path attacker in the KEV reports therefore needs a trusted certificate, which is the basis for AC:H."
          },
          "locations": [
